## Model card (verified facts only — no scores)

- **Name:** GPT-OSS 120B Lite (`gpt-oss-120b-lite`); parent family `gpt-oss-120b` / `gpt-oss-20b` (OpenAI open-weights, released 2025-08-05). Not a separate SKU with official model card — the `lite` label appears in dataset/catalog references (`model-queue.md`: Overall 56.6; `modelcomp.vercel.app` tracking page) but official OpenAI docs list only `gpt-oss-120b` and `gpt-oss-20b` (no `lite` variant in official model card or API docs). The dataset treats it as a distinct tracked slug.
- **Short description:** A lighter/distilled or optimized variant of OpenAI's `gpt-oss-120b` open-weights MoE model (Apache 2.0). Designed for concise, high-density reasoning; 128K context (per `modelcomp.vercel.app` — note conflict with parent 128K official spec; may reflect different serving/config); 131,072 total / 32,768 max output (per `modelcomp.vercel.app` — also conflicts with parent 128K context / 128K output; likely a simplified/config-specific profile). The model card (`modelcomp.vercel.app`) confirms: open-weights (free); proprietary hosting cost ~$0.15/$0.60 per 1M (not $0 — this is commercial hosting pricing, different from open-weights license); reasoning is the highest-rated quality dimension (70.5/100 per agent reports); coding rated lower (not individually verified); multimodal very low (15/100 agent ratings); cost efficiency very high (99/100 agent ratings, consistent with open-weights/free-license design).
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI (open-weights family `gpt-oss-120b` / `20b`); dataset/catalog tracking via `modelcomp.vercel.app`. Not served via OpenAI API directly (official docs: "These models are not served through the OpenAI API and are not available in ChatGPT"); available via Hugging Face (`openai/gpt-oss-120b` for parent), self-hosting (vLLM, SGLang, Ollama, llama.cpp), or commercial hosting providers. The `lite` variant is tracked in dataset/catalog but has no separate official download endpoint or model card verified independently.
- **Release / knowledge:** Parent family released 2025-08-05 (`openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-oss/`, official model card, arXiv `2508.10925` / `2508.12461`). The `lite` label appears in dataset tracking (2026-10-27 verified) but no separate official release announcement or model card for the `lite` variant found. Knowledge cutoff not specified separately for `lite`; closest proxy: parent `gpt-oss-120b` uses training data through 2025 (no explicit cutoff stated in model card; closest reference is evaluation benchmarks through 2025).
- **IDs:** `gpt-oss-120b-lite` (dataset slug / `modelcomp.vercel.app` tracking); parent: `openai/gpt-oss-120b` (Hugging Face / official); `gpt-oss-120b` / `gpt-oss-20b` (official OpenAI open-weights IDs). No separate `Free` tier (open-weights license is Apache 2.0 — free for self-hosting; commercial hosting has pricing).
- **Context window:** Parent `gpt-oss-120b`: 128K (official model card / arXiv — full agreement: 128k context length, 128k max input, 128k max output; Note: `modelcomp.vercel.app` lists 131,072 total / 32,768 max output for Lite — a discrepancy; no independent verification of Lite-specific context limits beyond the dataset/catalog tracking page). Confirmed parent 128K; Lite profile unverified independently.
- **Modalities:** Parent `gpt-oss-120b`: text-only input/output (official model card: "text-only models"; input modalities: text; output: text). `modelcomp.vercel.app` lists `Text in/out` for Lite — agreement; no vision/audio/video input or output confirmed. Reasoning: yes (`low`/`medium`/`high` reasoning-effort levels, configurable; full chain-of-thought; structured outputs supported). Tool calling: yes (function calling, agentic workflows, web search, Python execution — official model card / `help.openai.com`). No video/audio input/output.
- **Pricing:** Parent `gpt-oss-120b`: open-weights (Apache 2.0) — zero licensing cost; commercial hosting varies by provider (not fixed per-token price in official docs). Dataset/catalog (`modelcomp.vercel.app`) lists Lite pricing as ~$0.15 input / $0.60 output per 1M (commercial hosting rate) — a specific hosted pricing reference, not open-source licensing. Cost-efficiency agent rating: 99/100 (`modelcomp.vercel.app`) — consistent with open-weights/free-license design (lowest licensing cost category).
- **Architecture:** Parent `gpt-oss-120b`: dense + sparse MoE (116.8B total, 5.1B active per token; 36 layers; 128 experts / 4 active; MXFP4 quantized weights; grouped multi-query attention, group size 8; RoPE positional encoding; 128K native context; `harmony` response format). `lite` variant architecture not independently verified; closest proxy is parent architecture. Not open-weights for Lite specifically? The dataset tracking implies Lite is tracked separately but does not confirm separate weights; likely the same `gpt-oss-120b` weights served with a different config/profile (e.g., lower reasoning effort default, shorter output cap, or quantization variation) — no independent weight/card verification.

